The toolkit contains generalized Fractal/MIDI procedures and qualified hardware
observations. Application documentation copies, chat histories, personal preset
backups, credentials and private device names are not distributed.

The FM9 12.00 amp roster contains recorded numeric ID/name pairs with source
provenance. Manufacturer manuals and third-party implementations are linked;
their manuals have not been vendored. The contained C# framing, assembly,
stored decoder and fixture technique are modified Apache-2.0 PresetMaestro
source. See docs/protocol-release.json for origin revision, file hashes and
modifications.

The reviewed amplifier catalogue generalizes PresetMaestro's Apache-2.0 factual
identities, explicit family groups and original qualifications. Source file
hashes and research locators accompany the dataset. Only factual identities,
review notes and reading links are distributed; community guide prose, images
and user-supplied research tables are not redistributed. Ampdex and the Fractal
Wiki share source lineage and are not independent confirmations. Exact revision
claims retain their uncertainty. The recorded device roster superseded an older
candidate table derived from MCP MIDI Control / fractal-syx-codec; that candidate
table and upstream runtime code are not included here.

