The block identity catalogue retains factual enum IDs, display names and dated
model instance counts researched from Fractal Audio MIDI revision 1.4, Blocks
Guide June 2023 and the pinned Apache-2.0 Gen-3 implementation credited above.
Source revisions, SHA-256 and authority/model limits accompany the JSON data.
Manufacturer prose, full manuals and unrelated upstream source are not bundled.

The contained audio parameter catalogue derives factual editor IDs, symbols and
qualified display hints from each model's params.ts at MCP MIDI Control revision
59047175cfc4f23e092931b54a7c54f2bffde3ea (Apache-2.0, Stephen Staker, credited above).
Saved audio field and grid-mask facts derive from that revision's presetBody.ts
and corroborating gridLayout.ts commentary. Dataset entries retain inference
qualifications; source hashes and model scopes accompany the catalogue and
protocol release. These facts do not establish new hardware compatibility.

The saved-image edit writer is an inverse of the contained Huffman/container
decoder. General scene-state and channel-row offsets use the pinned presetBody.ts
format research credited above; docs/preset-editing-validation.json retains its
source hash and synthetic validation boundary. No normal build fetch is required.

