The original licence/notice is retained in docs/big-saurus-license.txt. Changes
include field selection, alias deduplication, neutral provenance summaries and
explicit model/firmware/shape constraints. Source hashes and limitations accompany
the catalogue. Upstream-reported hardware observations are not toolkit validation.

Native MIDI now uses the independently versioned MightBeUseful.Midi and
MightBeUseful.Midi.Windows 0.3.4 packages from MIDIHelperLibrary.
See dependencies/midi/manifest.json for exact package hashes and source revision,
and dependencies/midi/README.md for third-party package provenance and licences.
These binary dependencies do not replace the contained Fractal protocol sources.

Native macOS MIDI uses MightBeUseful.Midi.CoreMidi 0.3.4 and its standard
DryWetMIDI 8.0.3 backend. The contained package preserves upstream native assets
and licence notices; see dependencies/midi/licenses and the dependency manifest.
No native Mac hardware qualification is implied by portable offline checks.
